# Slice 333: g is the function `fn: g merge(f)` creates at the root. The statements `g(1; 2)` and `g(3; 4)` (in pair)
# apply it with two actuals, `g(b := 7; a := 6)` binds them by name: f is never called (f_calls 0, f_last 0), g's own
# data counts three calls and keeps the last 67.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int (int: calls 0; int: last 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    last := a * 10 + b
    return: last
end: f
fn: g merge(f)
g(1; 2)
fn: pair (int: x) int
    g(3; 4)
    return: x + 1
end: pair
int: r pair(5)
g(b := 7; a := 6)
int: f_calls f\data\calls
int: f_last f\data\last
int: g_calls g\data\calls
int: g_last g\data\last
